normally|PASS: Usual-opening schedule and normally-functioning door represent frequency versus expected manner; both translations preserve the exception or restoration.
south|PASS: Direction noun, window adjective and turn-direction adverb have clear syntax; cardinal-capitalization qualification avoids inventing a proper region.
weave|REVIEW: [GRAMMAR] Fabric wove/woven and motion weaved are reviewed as different inflection patterns; local source supports both meanings but movement-form evidence needs lexical corroboration.
cookie|PASS: Sweet baked food noun matches plural oatmeal biscuits; American cookie/British biscuit note is qualified and does not claim every biscuit is a cookie.
forward|REVIEW: [POS_CLASSIFICATION] Direction adverb and front-section adjective are supported; 4600 PREPOSITION label conflicts with its own adverbial example and is not authored as a new Sense.
